-- `l4 lts` over the lifecycle nouns written as anchors and as values
-- (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §2.6 card B1). Read by jl4/tests/LtsList.hs,
-- case `lifecycle-anchors`; the golden is examples/lts/expected/.
--
-- Alice signs at 8 in every trace. The first three rules all fall due at
-- 13: OF THE JOIN and OF (THE JOIN) are 8 + 5, and OF (THE ARMING) is the
-- arming of the obligation the delivery continues, which its trace starts
-- at 3, plus 10. A noun anchor is the same anchor whether bare or
-- bracketed, and the list dates all three. The
-- fourth falls due at 13 as well, but its anchor does arithmetic on the
-- noun, and the list does not work that out: it says the deadline is not
-- known here (doc/reference/regulative/lts-list.md).

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor

alice MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`noun anchor` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY alice MUST Deliver alice WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bracketed noun` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY alice MUST Deliver alice WITHIN 5 OF (THE JOIN))

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bracketed arming` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY alice MUST Deliver alice WITHIN 10 OF (THE ARMING))

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`arithmetic on the noun` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY alice MUST Deliver alice WITHIN 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 5))

#TRACE `noun anchor` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8

#TRACE `bracketed noun` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8

#TRACE `bracketed arming` AT 3 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8

#TRACE `arithmetic on the noun` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
